diagnosis_text:
Affected component: OSPF virtual-link adjacency (VLINK0) that stitches the two OSPF domains together. The virtual link is configured between the ABRs r4 and r8, over transit area 1, to extend the backbone (area 0) across the r5–r8 side.

Mechanism: After the box restart, OSPF on r8 tried to bring up the virtual link before it had usable reachability across the transit area. When the underlay (area 1) path to r4 was not yet in the RIB, packets for the virtual link’s neighbor were unroutable, so OSPF control traffic over VLINK0 failed. That temporarily blackholed traffic that needed to cross the backbone via the virtual link.

