is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r8
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: OSPF virtual-link adjacency (VLINK0) that stitches the two OSPF domains together. The virtual link is configured between the ABRs r4 and r8, over transit area 1, to extend the backbone (area 0) across the r5–r8 side.

Mechanism: After the box restart, OSPF on r8 tried to bring up the virtual link before it had usable reachability across the transit area. When the underlay (area 1) path to r4 was not yet in the RIB, packets for the virtual link’s neighbor were unroutable, so OSPF control traffic over VLINK0 failed. That temporarily blackholed traffic that needed to cross the backbone via the virtual link.

Localization: 
- r8 OSPF log shows: “sendmsg in ospf_write failed to 45.1.1.1, interface VLINK0 … Network is unreachable” (r8 /var/log/frr/frr.log). 45.1.1.1 is r4’s area 1 address.
- r4 and r8 both have “area 1 virtual-link …” configured (r4 RID 14.1.4.1; r8 RID 18.1.4.1). Current state is healthy: both ends show the VLINK0 neighbor Full (show ip ospf neighbor detail on r4 and r8).

Root cause: r8’s ospfd formed the virtual link before area 1 reachability to r4 (45.1.1.1) existed after the restart, making the virtual link temporarily unroutable.

Corrective fix: Ensure OSPF on r8 starts only after interfaces/area 1 adjacencies are up (e.g., add a service/startup delay or dependency), or add a minimal static route in r8 towards r4’s area 1 next-hop to cover bootstrapping. Longer term, avoid dependence on virtual links for backbone continuity if possible. The link is currently restored and stable. 
=== END ===